{"availability":"available","full":"mhju0/fullcourt","name":"fullcourt","description":"An NBA schedule website for comparing how much rest teams get and how far they travel between games, with matchup views that make schedule differences easier to see","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-03-30T01:51:45Z","updated":"2026-10-06T15:42:36Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://fullcourt-nba.vercel.app","topics":["basketball-analytics","data-pipeline","data-visualization","drizzle-orm","machine-learning","nba","nextjs","postgresql","predictive-modeling","python","react","scikit-learn","sports-analytics","supabase","tailwindcss","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://fullcourt-nba.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:45:46.885Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T15:45:46.885Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T15:45:46.885Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:45:46.885Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["NBA rest and schedule findings, player shooting splits, and source-linked officiating reports.","FullCourt scores each team's schedule load, compares the two teams in a matchup, and measures how often the more-rested side won. It also examines playoff series, player shooting, shot locations, missing rotation players, and officiating patterns.","Home court matters much more than rest. The regular-season model makes a call when the more-rested team is at home; rested visitors are reported separately. Both win rates are compared with their venue baselines. These are historical associations, not estimates of what rest alone caused or a complete forecast of who will win."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mhju0/fullcourt/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d264720b98a681cd08aa5fd55359351006936819002d084407e9144f1e6cfb58","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T15:45:47.139Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:45:47.139Z",